+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool input against the tool's declared JSON Schema before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` describing what failed rather than throwing so the model can correct a malformed call on a subsequent round. Only an unregistered tool name throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and does not invoke the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L12)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only: valid input carrying an unlisted extra property is passed through to the executor unchanged, without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults.
+- When a field has the wrong type, the rejection message and log output name the failing property path and expected type and never include any property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the property path and expected type without leaking any input value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+- When the model emits a malformed tool call during an orchestrated turn, the orchestrator feeds the rejection `ToolResponse` back as the `tool_result` so the model can correct and retry within `maxToolRounds` without aborting `processMessage` ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the provider as a tool_result so a corrected retry resolves processMessage](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when called with an unregistered tool name.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at `register` time; an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with a message that names the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws synchronously at register time when the inputSchema is uncompilable and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L85)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object identity.
